            <div xml:id="d536">

                <pb facs="0629" n="371" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg371"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1028</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10 a. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s 16th. Adjudication by prize-claims committee does not supplant
                    remedy provided in Order V, rule 2, of prize court rules. Committee considers
                    exclusively equity claims of ship repairers, mortgagees and like against ships
                    or cargoes already finally dealt with by prize court, who are deprived of
                    ordinary remedies and cannot appear in ordinary proceedings.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
